{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1534092-aspirations-and-touchstones-a-unified-framework-of-story-drivers","id":1534092,"title":"Aspirations and Touchstones: a unified framework of story drivers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-12T03:25:36-07:00","id":1534092,"title":"Aspirations and Touchstones: a unified framework of story drivers","content":"<br /> First of all, please consider this post more like general reflections and ramblings about RPG design rather than actual homebrew to use in practice.<br /> <br /> In my experience as both player and ST in a few CofD games, I have seen several different approaches that players had with Aspirations and Touchstones.<br /> <br /> In some games, each player had their own Aspirations with their own very personal goals, so much so that the PCs would mostly go do their own stuff and not cooperate much with each other. In several other games, all players would have similar Aspirations related to pursuing whatever &quot;main plot&quot; the chronicle had. Basically, they would all share at least one Group Aspiration.<br /> <br /> In many games, players didn't care about Touchstones. They would interact with them the bare minimum and only when strictly necessary, for example for healing Clarity (and often they had objects or places as Touchstones). A couple of chronicles, however, had the story spring because all players were invested in a common element, whether it was a place or a creature, that kinda acted like a Group Touchstone.<br /> <br /> Then I also run a Deviant game. Deviant is particular compared to other splats because instead of Aspirations, characters have 5 Touchstones. Because all characters were Remade by the same Conspiracy (for the sake of simplicity), several Conviction Touchstones were shared among characters (they basically had Group Touchstones), and players seemed to be very invested in their Touchstones.<br /> <br /> All of this leads me to think that Aspirations and Touchstones are, for some aspects, fundamentally the same, in the sense that they are <b><i>story drivers</i></b>.<br /> Pursuing Conviction Touchstones and defending Loyalty Touchstones is the main drive of a Deviant chronicle, in the same way that pursuing Aspirations is one of the main ways to drive a story forward in most game lines. In this sense (and ignoring other aspects), they are almost interchangeable, as long as they are things that keep the players engaged, push characters to act, add conflict to the story and ultimately, grant Beats.<br /> <br /> (as a note, I will add that personally I always prefer to use Group Beats in my games)<br /> <br /> Because each player and each troupe is different, some players may be more interested in some components of the game than others. Some prefer more personal stories, some just follow the group, some are more proactive, some are more reactive, some want to have meaningful, intimate roleplaying with NPCs, some just care about investigating a mystery and complex plots, etc.<br /> <br /> So instead of having a fixed set of Aspirations and Touchstones, that players may not even be interested in, each group (or even, each player) should be able to decide how to engage the story.<br /> <br /> Imagine if each character had 5 Slots that could each be filled with one of the following:<br /> - Personal Aspiration<br /> - Group Aspiration (i.e. an Aspiration that PCs share and pursue together as a group. For example, whatever &quot;main plot&quot; the chronicle might have, if any)<br /> - Personal Touchstone<br /> - Group Touchstone (NPCs, objects or places that the whole group is invested in. For example, a pack's Totem, or a shared Safe Place, or an NPC all characters are related with)<br /> <br /> During Session 0 the troupe should decide together how they want to fill the slots. The choice of how the slots are filled will shape the type of game players want. If all players fill the slots with Personal Aspirations and Touchstones, then games will obviously be very character-driven and personal to each character. Group Aspirations and Touchstones tell the ST that players want to pursue objectives as a group, which may be suited for games like Werewolf or Geist that have a major focus on the pack and krewe as a whole. Touchstones might show a player's interest in relationships, for example, while another player might not care.<br /> <br /> Yes, I know that this kind of system would completely break how Touchstones and Aspirations currently work in the games, especially Deviant. As I said, this is more a general idea than something to use in practice. But I kinda wish there was a way to tailor <i>story drivers</i> (and Beat generators) to whatever best suits a group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-17T15:36:14-08:00","id":1547116,"title":"","content":"I absolutely love the thoughts you're developing here.<br /> I'm currently preparing a chronicle where my players start out as baseline humans, make a short detour of being Hunters and become Deviants in the aftermath.<br /> <br /> One problem I still haven't solved is to handle the transition from one system to another regarding Touchstones and Aspirations.<br /> Your idea of abstracting them to story drivers is a good one.<br /> I mean, story-wise, there's no real difference between a Conviction Touchstone &quot;Ed from the lab&quot; and an Aspiration like &quot;Get revenge on Ed from the lab&quot;.<br /> <br /> So I think about following your proposal and - when the time comes to apply the Deviant template - to ask my players to select not 5 Touchstones but 5 Story Drivers, either Touchstones or Aspirations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1534092-aspirations-and-touchstones-a-unified-framework-of-story-drivers#post1534092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I know that this kind of system would completely break how Touchstones and Aspirations currently work in the games, especially Deviant.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you don't mind, can you elaborate on what you mean specifically?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6817-quinn","name":"Quinn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-18T14:05:04-08:00","id":1547134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1534092-aspirations-and-touchstones-a-unified-framework-of-story-drivers?p=1547116#post1547116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, story-wise, there's no real difference between a Conviction Touchstone &quot;Ed from the lab&quot; and an Aspiration like &quot;Get revenge on Ed from the lab&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, exactly. In Deviant, Touchstones blur the line between the thing that gives you Beats, the thing that gives you Willpower, and the thing that heals your Stability. But at the end, they all serve the same purpose of driving the story. &quot;Make progress in pursuit of a Conviction Touchstone&quot; is just a set Aspiration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1534092-aspirations-and-touchstones-a-unified-framework-of-story-drivers?p=1547116#post1547116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One problem I still haven't solved is to handle the transition from one system to another regarding Touchstones and Aspirations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am also preparing a Changeling Chronicle where the players will play as mortals for a few stories and then go through the Durance.<br /> What I do is to add Bonds to the mortal character sheets. Bonds are essentially the Mortal version of Touchstones: they are people (or places and objects, but preferably NPCs) that the characters have strong ties to and care about. They can have up to three Bonds, that they might fill up in the course of the first stories depending on which NPCs they get more attached to.<br /> <br /> Once they get transformed into splats, one or more Bonds will become their Touchstone(s).<br /> <br /> You can add some other effect to Bonds, perhaps giving a bonus on Integrity rolls if they have a meaningful interaction; or you can reward a Beat or Willpower if they take a risk or suffer for a Bond just like a Loyalty Touchstone would.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quinn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1534092-aspirations-and-touchstones-a-unified-framework-of-story-drivers?p=1547116#post1547116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't mind, can you elaborate on what you mean specifically?</div> </div> </div> </div>For Deviant especially everything revolves around Touchstones, and they are also tied to Origins. In my suggested framework, each character has 5 Slots and the players choose how to fill them with Personal/Group Touchstones or Aspirations. For example, imagine if a player chooses to have 1 Group Aspiration, 1 Personal Aspiration, 1 Group Touchstone and 2 Personal Touchstones.<br /> How would Origins provide +1 Conviction or Loyalty? Would the Stability healing work with Aspirations? How would Faltering, Catharsis, Switching Sides etc. work with only 3 Touchstones ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-29T15:01:25-08:00","id":1547313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1534092-aspirations-and-touchstones-a-unified-framework-of-story-drivers?p=1547134#post1547134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Deviant especially everything revolves around Touchstones, and they are also tied to Origins. In my suggested framework, each character has 5 Slots and the players choose how to fill them with Personal/Group Touchstones or Aspirations. For example, imagine if a player chooses to have 1 Group Aspiration, 1 Personal Aspiration, 1 Group Touchstone and 2 Personal Touchstones.<br /> How would Origins provide +1 Conviction or Loyalty? Would the Stability healing work with Aspirations? How would Faltering, Catharsis, Switching Sides etc. work with only 3 Touchstones ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the explanation. I think that most of it could be solved by tying &quot;Story Drivers&quot; to Conviction or Loyalty.<br /> <br /> But the more I think of it, my approach to use parts of your idea doesn't make much difference. <i>If</i> an Aspiration is tied to either Conviction or Loyalty, it might just as well be expressed as a Touchstone in game terms. Which is pretty much the complementary observation of yours:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwhisper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1534092-aspirations-and-touchstones-a-unified-framework-of-story-drivers?p=1547134#post1547134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Make progress in pursuit of a Conviction Touchstone&quot; is just a set Aspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'll encourage (but not force) my players to use Aspirations for things that aren't tied to the Conviction/Loyalty dichotomy, but to develop other aspects of the character or the story. Maybe then the distinction in the mechanics has an equivalent in the story.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6817-quinn","name":"Quinn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}